From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] usb: configfs: don't queue unused gadget state uevents

The Android Auto daemon listens for the f_accessory ACCESSORY=START event.
It does not consume configfs USB_STATE notifications. Avoid scheduling the
legacy android_work callback on USB control requests/disconnects; its worker
was reported in-flight during a per-CPU events workqueue lockup on the Orange
Pi 6.18.58 build. The captured output did not include a stack trace, so this
patch is a mitigation hypothesis rather than a confirmed root-cause fix.

---
 drivers/usb/gadget/configfs.c | 8 --------
 1 file changed, 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/configfs.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/configfs.c
index aaaa00000000..bbbb11111111 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/configfs.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/configfs.c
@@ -1961,6 +1961,5 @@ static int android_setup(struct usb_gadget *gadget,
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&cdev->lock, flags);
 	if (!gi->connected) {
 		gi->connected = 1;
-		schedule_work(&gi->work);
 	}
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&cdev->lock, flags);
@@ -1983,6 +1983,0 @@ static int android_setup(struct usb_gadget *gadget,
-	spin_lock_irqsave(&cdev->lock, flags);
-	if (c->bRequest == USB_REQ_SET_CONFIGURATION &&
-						cdev->config) {
-		schedule_work(&gi->work);
-	}
-	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&cdev->lock, flags);
@@ -2050,6 +2050,5 @@ static void configfs_composite_disconnect(struct usb_gadget *gadget)
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_UEVENT
 	gi->connected = 0;
-	schedule_work(&gi->work);
 #endif
 	composite_disconnect(gadget);
